# The discrete card is not the seat's: the panel is on the iGPU and the
# compositor is pinned to it (98-nova-igpu.rules, fact 1), so nothing on the
# desktop should ever hold the card. Only its card node loses the tags; the
# render node keeps them, and PRIME offload uses that and /dev/nvidia*.
#
# Without the "seat" tag logind does not track the node, and TakeDevice on it
# fails with ENODEV. That is the point: aquamarine opens a GPU that appears
# while the compositor runs through logind, ignoring AQ_DRM_DEVICES and the
# seat, and keeps it until logout. One plug-in in a session that started on
# battery was enough for every later unplug to leave the card powered (fact 53).
#
# After 71-seat.rules, which adds the tags.
SUBSYSTEM=="drm", KERNEL=="card[0-9]*", ENV{DEVTYPE}=="drm_minor", \
  SUBSYSTEMS=="pci", ATTRS{vendor}=="0x10de", \
  ATTR{[dmi/id]product_version}=="ThinkPad P1 Gen 4i", \
  TAG-="seat", TAG-="master-of-seat"
